@startuml state-find
'' PlantUML over Mermaid because the find bar is a small finite-state machine with a count-parameterised
'' state, self-looping cycle transitions, and a Stale state reached by an external event (the document
'' changing underneath the painted Ranges); PlantUML state diagrams give parameterised states,
'' self-transitions, and per-state colour. Literal palette hexes: blue-violet #7590DB ephemeral :ui/find,
'' green #67B11D the "matches present" (painted) state, amber #B1951D stale, grey for hidden.
!include _vv-theme.iuml

title Find-bar state machine (:ui/find)\n{:visible? :query :count :idx :gen}

skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor APPDB_TINT
}

[*] --> Hidden

state "Hidden" as Hidden #DDDDDD : visible? = false\nhighlights cleared  ·  **query REMEMBERED**
state "Visible (empty)" as Empty APPDB_TINT : visible? = true\nquery = ""  ·  count = 0
state "Debouncing" as Debounce #C7CFE8 : a keystroke landed\n:gen++ · [:find/run gen] scheduled 100 ms out
state "Visible (matches: n)" as Matches MARKDOWN_TINT : visible? = true\ncount = n > 0  ·  <latex>\mathit{idx} \in 1..n</latex>\nhighlights painted
state "Stale" as Stale #E8DCA8 : the DOM changed under the Ranges\n(live refresh · streamed append ·\nMathJax/mermaid post-pass · PDF text layer)

Hidden  --> Empty   : open  /  [:find/toggle]\n(query = "")
Hidden  --> Debounce : open with a REMEMBERED query\n/ [:find/toggle] → :find/search
Empty   --> Hidden  : toggle off | Escape\n/ [:find/close] → clear!

Empty    --> Debounce : type  /  [:find/set-query]
Matches  --> Debounce : edit the query
Debounce --> Debounce : another keystroke\n(:gen++ — the older run is dropped)
Debounce --> Matches  : [:find/result] with count n > 0\n**only if gen is still current**
Debounce --> Empty    : [:find/result] with count = 0

Matches --> Matches : cycle  [:find/cycle ±1]\nF3 / Shift+F3  ·  vim n / N  (see note)

Matches --> Stale   : MutationObserver fires
Stale   --> Matches : next search/cycle → **ensure-fresh!**\nre-collect, clamp the cursor
Stale   --> Empty   : re-collect finds nothing

Matches --> Hidden  : Escape / ×  [:find/close]\n→ clear! (delete both highlights)
Matches --> Hidden  : toggle off
Matches --> Empty   : **a different document or facet**\n[:find/reset] (watches :ui/find-context)

note bottom of Matches #FFF6D6
  cycle! wraps with modular arithmetic. Internally the cursor is
  0-based and steps by <latex>\mathit{dir} \in \{+1, -1\}</latex>:
  <latex>\mathit{idx} := (\mathit{idx} + \mathit{dir}) \bmod n</latex>
  Forward is therefore, in the 1-based index the UI shows as "idx/n":
  <latex>\mathit{idx} := (\mathit{idx} \bmod n) + 1</latex>
  and backward is:
  <latex>\mathit{idx} := ((\mathit{idx} - 2) \bmod n) + 1</latex>

  Under a MODAL keymap, Enter does not cycle — it COMMITS, returning
  the keyboard to normal mode while the bar and highlights stay, so
  that n / N (bare printable keys) can reach the resolver at all.
end note

legend right
  |= Colour |= State / concept |
  |<#DDDDDD>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| Hidden (bar closed, highlights cleared, query kept) |
  |<#7590DB>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| Visible, no current matches (app-db :ui/find) |
  |<#C7CFE8>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| Debouncing — a newer generation supersedes an older run |
  |<#67B11D>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| Visible with painted matches (CSS highlights) |
  |<#E8DCA8>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| Stale — the DOM moved under the Ranges |
endlegend
@enduml
